{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sure-starred-springtail","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Operator directive (verbatim, 2026-08-13)\n'add standing guidance for the project: flaky tests get debugged using rebar-debug, not retried until they pass. a flaky CI pipeline is a failure that slows development, wastes tokens, and decreases our trust in CI as a regression oracle.'\n\n## Context (tonight's evidence)\nThe order-dependent leaked-logger flake (future-fibroid-hammerkop) cost four Verified -1s across changes 1715/1716/1717/1720, multiple recheck cycles, and hours of queued rebases before it was root-caused (deterministic RED via a two-file pytest invocation) and fixed class-wide (change 1721). Root-causing it once was cheaper than every recheck combined.\n\n## Work\n- Add the rule to AGENTS.md as concise agent guidance (respect that file's lean style): a test that fails intermittently is a BUG to root-cause — reproduce deterministically (e.g. via the /rebar-debug worktree workflow), fix the class, and only then re-run CI; 'recheck' is reserved for provably environmental faults (e.g. TLS/promisor cert flake) with the reasoning stated in the recheck comment.\n- Reconcile with the existing CI -1 triage playbook so the two don't conflict: recheck-with-reasoning remains valid for infra faults; test-nondeterminism is never 'recheck until green'.\n- Cross-link any docs home for CI triage rather than duplicating.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] AGENTS.md carries the rule with the rationale compressed to one sentence (slows development, wastes tokens, erodes CI as a regression oracle).\n- [ ] The guidance names the deterministic-reproduction expectation and the narrow legitimate-recheck carve-out.\n- [ ] One authoritative wording; docs cross-linked not duplicated.","id":"9b79-56ba-0d16-4c49","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Guidance: flaky tests get debugged, not retried"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786616470523047001,"uuid":"4cd8b5b2-4b3f-4298-aed2-2712f93ae0bd"}